---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { rates, gbp } from '../data/rates';

const TURNSTILE_SITEKEY = '0x4AAAAAAEcCwzuExy2fSCmH';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Hire Me to Speak | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="Keynotes, private talks and workshops by Saielle DaSilva on building intentional products, designing humane AI, and leading through uncertainty."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Speaking &amp; workshops</p>
      <h1>Keynotes and workshops that change what Monday looks like.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Public keynotes and private company sessions about building
        intentional products, designing humane AI and leading through
        uncertainty.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why people ask me to speak</h2>
      <p>
        A good keynote changes the way a room thinks. A great one changes
        what a team does on Monday morning. I have given talks at Mind the
        Product, Turing Fest and Business of Software, and run workshops for
        product and design organisations through the shift into data and AI.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is plenty of "inspiration" available, and conferences are full
        of it. I am not selling motivation. I am selling a shared mental
        model you can actually use, delivered in a voice that does not put
        your team to sleep.
      </p>

      <h2>Sound familiar?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your team came back from a conference buzzing, then nothing changed.</li>
        <li>Everyone uses AI, but nobody can say when it helps versus when it is a crutch.</li>
        <li>People say your culture is the problem, but nobody can name the decisions that made it that way.</li>
        <li>You keep making the same product decisions because there is no shared idea of what "good" means.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <p>
        Keynotes for public events and private talks for companies. The
        content is the same craft: naming the decisions behind strong
        products and humane teams. The format is the difference between
        inspiring a room and building capability in your teams.
      </p>

      <h3>Public keynotes</h3>
      <p>
        Forty to sixty minutes. A single, memorable argument your audience
        repeats afterwards. Talks on intention, humane AI, product culture
        and leading through uncertainty. This is where ideas like designing
        AI as a thinking partner, not a writing service, get their name.
      </p>

      <h3>Private talks and workshops</h3>
      <p>
        Half or full day. Not a lecture. The same frameworks applied to your
        actual problems: your teams, your AI choices, your culture.
        Hands-on, interactive and specific. This is for companies that need
        more than somebody in a nice suit to talk at their all-hands.
      </p>

      <h2>What you get</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A talk your people can actually use, not just applaud</li>
        <li>Frameworks your team keeps using after I have gone</li>
        <li>Straight answers about AI, product and culture with no vendor agenda</li>
        <li>From {gbp(rates.speaking)} for an event. Private workshops quoted by scope and travel.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        Tell me the audience and the outcome you want. I shape the talk to
        fit. For public events, we agree a title and abstract. For private
        work, we talk about what your team is actually wrestling with before
        I disappear to prepare.
      </p>
      <p>
        I do not use slides as a crutch, I am not a motivational act, and I
        will not pretend your industry's hard problems are simple. What you
        get instead is a talk that respects the room enough to ask something
        of it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="contact-form-section" aria-label="Book a talk">
      <div class="contact-card">
        <h2>Let's talk.</h2>
        <p class="form-lede">
          Whether it is a keynote for your event or a workshop for your team,
          tell me the audience and the outcome you want.
        </p>
        <form id="contact-form" novalidate>
          <input type="hidden" name="source" value="speaking" />
          <div class="form-grid">
            <label>
              <span class="form-label">Name</span>
              <input type="text" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
            </label>
            <label>
              <span class="form-label">Email</span>
              <input type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
            </label>
          </div>
          <label>
            <span class="form-label">What's this about?</span>
            <select name="topic">
              <option value="strategic-direction">
                Strategic direction
              </option>
              <option value="execution">Execution &amp; transformation</option>
              <option value="fractional">Fractional leadership</option>
              <option value="speaking" selected>Speaking &amp; workshops</option>
              <option value="mentoring">Mentoring</option>
              <option value="other">Something else</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label>
            <span class="form-label">Message</span>
            <textarea name="message" rows="5" required></textarea>
          </label>
          {
            TURNSTILE_SITEKEY && (
              <>
                <div
                  class="cf-turnstile"
                  data-sitekey={TURNSTILE_SITEKEY}
                  data-theme="light"
                />
                <script
                  is:inline
                  src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js"
                  async
                  defer
                />
              </>
            )
          }
          <button class="btn-plain" type="submit">Send it</button>
          <p class="form-status" id="form-status" role="status"></p>
        </form>
      </div>
      <p class="faq-link">
        Questions first? <a href="/faq">Read the FAQ.</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>

  <script>
    const ENDPOINT = 'https://contact-form.intentionaut.workers.dev/contact';
    const form = document.getElementById('contact-form');

    form?.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const data = Object.fromEntries(new FormData(form));
      const statusEl = document.getElementById('form-status');

      try {
        const res = await fetch(ENDPOINT, {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(data),
        });
        const result = await res.json();
        if (res.ok) {
          form.reset();
          if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = result.message || "Thank you; I'll reply soon.";
        } else {
          if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = result.error || 'Something went wrong; please email me directly.';
        }
      } catch {
        if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = 'Something went wrong; please email me directly.';
      }
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
